    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0239" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/737a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Diplomatic Representatives in Allied Countries
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d219-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-18T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Please ascertain as promptly as possible the views of the Government to which you
                    are accredited in regard to the Pope’s recent peace communication. The above
                    information is desired by the President. Cable reply, which will be treated as
                    strictly confidential.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d219-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d219-f1-content">
                <p>Also to the Chargé in Siam, the Chargé in Rumania, and the Special Agent in
                    Corfu, Aug. 20, 4 p.m. (File No. 763.72119/742a.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
